{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavourIsDetermined","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavourIsDetermined","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.ud_letter_is_average","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.ud_letter_is_average","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L273-L282","doc":"**The `ud` letter is the average of the two crossings.** The shift `−h/2`\nsits exactly halfway, so the mixed-orientation entry of the typing table is\n`(σ + σ⁻¹)/2` and not a separate convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.skein_letter_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.skein_letter_inv","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L264-L271","doc":"**The `dd` letter is the inverse crossing.** Straight from the Hecke\nrelation `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1` of AGENTS.md §7a: multiplying by `σ⁻¹` gives\n`σ − σ⁻¹ = q − q⁻¹`, so the shift `d = −h` *is* `σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.two_shift_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.two_shift_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L230-L260","doc":"**The two-slot shift expansion.**\n\nIf two letters of a word each pick up the *same central* scalar `c`, the\ndifference of the shifted and unshifted words is a three-term combination of\nwords with one and both of those letters deleted:\n\n```\nX(a+c)Y(b+c)Z − XaYbZ = c·(XYbZ) + c·(XaYZ) + c²·(XYZ)\n```\n\nStated over a noncommutative `Ring` — the braid algebra is not commutative — with\ncentrality of `c` as an explicit hypothesis. Applied to the nucleons, `c` is the\nscalar `−h/2` and the three right-hand words are the proton word with one or\nboth flavour crossings smoothed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.nucleon_flip_retypes_two_of_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.nucleon_flip_retypes_two_of_three","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L224-L226","doc":"The proton case: **two** of the three crossings are retyped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.flip_retypes_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.flip_retypes_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L201-L222","doc":"**β-decay retypes TWO pairs.**\n\nA nucleon of `m+1` ups and `n` downs becomes one of `m` ups and `n+1` downs when\na single up flips. The flipped quark belonged to `m` same-flavour pairs and `n`\nmixed pairs, so:\n\n* `m` pairs move `uu → ud`;\n* `n` pairs move `ud → dd`;\n* the `C(m,2) + C(n,2)` pairs not containing it are untouched.\n\nStated additively to avoid truncated `ℕ` subtraction. At `m = n = 1` — the\nproton — this is `1 + 1 = 2` retyped crossings out of three, which is what the\ncensus chains show. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts_determined","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L192-L197","doc":"**Determination, stated plainly**: the shift multiset is a function of the\nquark counts, so two nucleon models with the same `(n_u, n_d)` cannot differ in\ntheir flavour letters. There is no flavour freedom to exploit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.nucleon_pairCounts_differ_by_one_uu_and_one_dd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.nucleon_pairCounts_differ_by_one_uu_and_one_dd","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L180-L190","doc":"**The pair-type counts differ by one `uu` and one `dd`.**\n\nGoing from the proton to the neutron removes one `uu` crossing and adds one\n`dd`, with the mixed-pair count unchanged. This is a statement about **counts**\nonly. It does *not* say the two words differ in one letter — see\n`flip_retypes_pairs`, which shows two crossings are retyped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.ud_count_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.ud_count_equal","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L173-L178","doc":"**The two nucleons share their mixed-pair count.**\n\nRead with `flip_retypes_pairs`: the equality is a **cancellation**, one `ud`\ngained against one `ud` lost, not evidence that the mixed crossings are\nuntouched by the decay. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts_sum","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L165-L171","doc":"**The typing is exhaustive**: the three pair types account for every pair of\nthe `n_u + n_d` quarks, so no crossing is left untyped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.succChooseTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.succChooseTwo","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L159-L163","doc":"`C(m+1, 2) = C(m, 2) + m`: adding one quark to a same-flavour group adds one\npair per quark already there. The `n = 1` case of `addChooseTwo`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.addChooseTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.addChooseTwo","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L147-L157","doc":"`C(m+n, 2) = C(m,2) + m·n + C(n,2)` — the `k = 2` case of Vandermonde,\nproved here because Mathlib carries no `Nat.add_choose_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.neutron_pairCounts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.neutron_pairCounts","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L143-L145","doc":"**The neutron `udd`**: no `uu`, two `ud`, one `dd` — the recipe's\n`[−h, −h/2, −h/2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.proton_pairCounts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.proton_pairCounts","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L139-L141","doc":"**The proton `uud`**: one `uu`, two `ud`, no `dd`. These are exactly the\nshifts the census recipe hardcodes as `[0, −h/2, −h/2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NucleonFlavour.pairCounts","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NucleonFlavourIsDetermined.lean#L133-L137","doc":"Pair-type counts for a three-quark content with `n_u` up and `n_d` down:\n`(#uu, #ud, #dd)`. Each unordered pair of quarks is one crossing, typed by the\ntwo orientations. ","signatureChunk":0}]}